  "narrative": "The eight metabolites converge on **Arachidonic Acid Metabolism (KEGG map00590)**, confirmed as a shared pathway for six of the eight compounds with a co-occurrence plausibility score of 1.00. The top-ranked drug-intervention pathways (Rofecoxib Action, Salicylate Action, Acetaminophen Action) all reflect the same underlying lipid cascade but are pharmacological labels; the biological anchor is arachidonic acid (AA, C00219).\n\n**Key driver compounds.** Arachidonic acid itself is the upstream precursor and driver. From it, the pathway branches into two major downstream arms: the **5-lipoxygenase (5-LOX) arm** producing 5-HETE (C04805) and Leukotriene A4 (C00909), and the **12/15-LOX arm** producing 15-HETE (C04742). The **CYP epoxygenase arm** yields 5,6-epoxy-8,11,14-eicosatrienoic acid (C14768), while the **cyclooxygenase (COX) arm** generates 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ₂ (C14717). KEGG reaction-path analysis confirms that arachidonic acid (C00219) is directly upstream of Leukotriene A4 (C00909) through the intermediate C05356 (bidirectional, 2 hops) and of 15-HETE (C04742) through intermediate C05966 (forward, 2 hops), establishing a verified upstream→downstream hierarchy.\n\n**Biological significance.** Coordinated elevation of 5-HETE and Leukotriene A4 signals 5-LOX activation, which drives leukotriene-mediated inflammation, bronchoconstriction, and neutrophil chemotaxis. Elevated 15-HETE reflects 12/15-LOX activity, associated with anti-inflammatory pro-resolving signaling and peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma (PPARγ) activation. 15d-PGJ₂ is a cyclopentenone prostaglandin that activates PPARγ and can trigger apoptosis in inflamed tissues. The simultaneous enrichment across all three LOX branches (5-, 12/15-, and CYP) suggests broad eicosanoid pathway activation rather than selective COX inhibition. The two non-eicosanoid compounds — 3,4-dihydroxybenzeneacetic acid and 4-hydroxybenzoic acid — fall outside the arachidonic acid cascade and may reflect parallel perturbations in gut-microbial aromatic metabolism or benzoate detoxification, warranting independent follow-up.",
